## 4. MOCK PATTERNS

### HTTP Mock
```xml
<munit-tools:mock-when doc:name="Mock HTTP" processor="http:request">
    <munit-tools:with-attributes>
        <munit-tools:with-attribute whereValue="{DOC_ID}" attributeName="doc:id"/>
    </munit-tools:with-attributes>
    <munit-tools:then-return>
        <munit-tools:payload 
            value='#[output application/json --- MunitTools::getResourceAsString("test-data/response.json")]' 
            encoding="UTF-8" mediaType="application/json"/>
        <munit-tools:attributes value="#[{statusCode: 200}]"/>
    </munit-tools:then-return>
</munit-tools:mock-when>
```

### HTTP Mock with Target Variable
```xml
<munit-tools:mock-when doc:name="Mock HTTP" processor="http:request">
