### ⚠️ Flow-Ref Mocking Anti-Pattern
<!-- Integrated: 2026-01-04 -->

**Problem:** Mocking flow-refs with `#[payload]` return causes empty payload during mock setup.

**Solution:** Avoid mocking internal flow-refs entirely. See Section 4.1 Mock Strategy Guide.

```xml
❌ AVOID - Causes "Unable to parse empty input" errors:
<munit-tools:mock-when processor="flow-ref">
    <munit-tools:then-return>
        <munit-tools:payload value="#[payload]"/>  <!-- Empty during setup! -->
    </munit-tools:then-return>
</munit-tools:mock-when>

✅ RECOMMENDED - Let flow-refs execute naturally:
<!-- No mock needed - connector mocks are sufficient -->
```

### Flow-Ref Mock (Variables Only - RARE)
<!-- Integrated: 2026-01-04 -->

**⚠️ WARNING:** Only for utility flows that ONLY set variables and have no business logic.

**Rule:** Never mock business flow-refs. Only mock external I/O connectors.

```xml
<munit-tools:mock-when doc:name="Mock Utility Subflow" processor="flow-ref">
    <munit-tools:with-attributes>
        <munit-tools:with-attribute whereValue="{DOC_ID}" attributeName="doc:id"/>
    </munit-tools:with-attributes>
    <munit-tools:then-return>
        <munit-tools:variables>
            <munit-tools:variable key="configValue" 
                value='#["test-value"]' 
                mediaType="application/json" encoding="UTF-8"/>
        </munit-tools:variables>
    </munit-tools:then-return>
</munit-tools:mock-when>
```

### Empty Mock (Void Operations)
```xml
<munit-tools:mock-when doc:name="Mock Publish" processor="solace:publish">
    <munit-tools:with-attributes>
        <munit-tools:with-attribute whereValue="{DOC_ID}" attributeName="doc:id"/>
    </munit-tools:with-attributes>
</munit-tools:mock-when>
```
**Use for:** `solace:publish`, `solace:ack`, `jms:publish`, `file:write`, `email:send`

### Solace Connector
```xml
<munit-tools:mock-when doc:name="Mock Solace Publish" processor="solace:publish">
    <munit-tools:with-attributes>
        <munit-tools:with-attribute whereValue="{DOC_ID}" attributeName="doc:id"/>
    </munit-tools:with-attributes>
</munit-tools:mock-when>

<munit-tools:mock-when doc:name="Mock Solace Ack" processor="solace:ack">
    <munit-tools:with-attributes>
        <munit-tools:with-attribute whereValue="{DOC_ID}" attributeName="doc:id"/>
    </munit-tools:with-attributes>
</munit-tools:mock-when>
```

