## 5. SPY PATTERNS

### Basic Spy (Field Assertions)
```xml
<munit-tools:spy doc:name="Spy Transform" processor="ee:transform">
    <munit-tools:with-attributes>
        <munit-tools:with-attribute whereValue="{DOC_ID}" attributeName="doc:id"/>
    </munit-tools:with-attributes>
    <munit-tools:before-call>
        <munit-tools:assert-that doc:name="Assert Input" 
            expression="#[payload]" is="#[MunitTools::notNullValue()]"/>
    </munit-tools:before-call>
    <munit-tools:after-call>
        <munit-tools:assert-that doc:name="Assert Output" 
            expression="#[payload.status]" is="#[MunitTools::equalTo('SUCCESS')]"/>
    </munit-tools:after-call>
</munit-tools:spy>
```

### Variable Verification Spy (RECOMMENDED for behavior testing)
```xml
<munit-tools:spy doc:name="Spy Variables" processor="ee:transform">
    <munit-tools:with-attributes>
        <munit-tools:with-attribute whereValue="{DOC_ID}" attributeName="doc:id"/>
    </munit-tools:with-attributes>
    <munit-tools:after-call>
        <!-- Verify variables are set correctly -->
        <munit-tools:assert-that expression="#[vars.sfdcObjectType]" is="#[MunitTools::equalTo('Contact')]"/>
        <munit-tools:assert-that expression="#[vars.sfdcRequestPayload]" is="#[MunitTools::notNullValue()]"/>
    </munit-tools:after-call>
</munit-tools:spy>
```

### File-Based Comparison Spy
```xml
<munit-tools:spy doc:name="Spy Mapping" processor="ee:transform">
    <munit-tools:with-attributes>
        <munit-tools:with-attribute whereValue="{DOC_ID}" attributeName="doc:id"/>
    </munit-tools:with-attributes>
    <munit-tools:after-call>
        <munit-tools:assert-equals doc:name="Assert Output"
            actual="#[payload]"
            expected='#[readUrl("classpath://test-data/expected-output.json", "application/json")]'
            message="Output mismatch"/>
    </munit-tools:after-call>
</munit-tools:spy>
```

**Rules:**
- ❌ NEVER create spies with only `notNullValue()` assertions
- ✅ ALWAYS verify actual values (use `equalTo`, `assert-equals`)
- ✅ Verify variables set by transforms
- Spies do NOT improve coverage - use for behavior validation

