## 6. ASSERTION PATTERNS

### Basic Assertions
| Assertion | Expression | Matcher |
|-----------|------------|---------|
| Not Null | `#[payload]` | `MunitTools::notNullValue()` |
| Equals | `#[payload.status]` | `MunitTools::equalTo('SUCCESS')` |
| Contains | `#[payload.message]` | `MunitTools::containsString('OK')` |
| Has Property | `#[payload]` | `MunitTools::hasProperty('status')` |
| Array Size | `#[sizeOf(payload.items)]` | `MunitTools::equalTo(5)` |
| Greater Than | `#[sizeOf(payload)]` | `MunitTools::greaterThan(0)` |

### Full Payload Comparison
```xml
<munit-tools:assert-equals doc:name="Assert Payload"
    actual="#[payload]"
    expected='#[output application/json --- readUrl("classpath://test-data/expected.json")]'
    message="Payload mismatch"/>

<munit-tools:assert-equals doc:name="Assert XML"
    actual="#[payload]"
    expected='#[readUrl("classpath://test-data/expected.xml", "application/xml")]'
    message="XML mismatch"/>
```

### Verify Processor Calls
```xml
<munit-tools:verify-call doc:name="Verify Called" processor="http:request" atLeast="#[1]">
    <munit-tools:with-attributes>
        <munit-tools:with-attribute whereValue="{DOC_ID}" attributeName="doc:id"/>
    </munit-tools:with-attributes>
</munit-tools:verify-call>
```

### JSON String Payloads
```xml
<!-- When payload is JSON string, parse before accessing fields -->
<munit-tools:assert-that expression="#[read(payload, 'application/json').status]" 
    is="#[MunitTools::equalTo('SUCCESS')]"/>
```

