## 9. TEST DATA PATTERNS

### File Structure
```
src/test/resources/test-data/
├── {flow}-input.json
├── {flow}-expected-output.json
├── http-response.json
├── db-results.json
└── sf-response.json
```

### XML Payload Pattern
```xml
<!-- ALWAYS include encoding and mediaType for XML payloads -->
<munit:payload 
    value='#[readUrl("classpath://test-data/input.xml", "application/xml")]' 
    encoding="UTF-8" 
    mediaType="application/xml"/>
```

### Rules
- ❌ No hardcoded dates
- ❌ No real credentials or PII
- ✅ Use TEST- prefixes for IDs
- ✅ XML payloads need `encoding="UTF-8" mediaType="application/xml"`

