## 10. POM CONFIGURATION

### Proven Versions
| Component | Version |
|-----------|---------|
| MUnit | 3.4.0 |
| Mule Maven Plugin | 4.5.1 |
| Maven Clean Plugin | 3.3.2 |

### Maven Commands
```bash
mvn clean test              # Standard run
mvn clean test -U           # Force update
mvn clean test -Dmunit.coverage.format=html  # With coverage
```

### MUnit Plugin Configuration with Parent POM
<!-- Integrated: 2026-01-04 -->

**Problem:** When inheriting from parent POM (e.g., `heineken-parent-pom`), adding `runtimeConfiguration` causes "Cannot convert 'MULE_EE' to Enum" error.

**Solution:** Use simple configuration. MUnit auto-discovers tests in `src/test/munit/` by default.

```xml
❌ BAD (Causes enum error with parent POM):
<plugin>
    <groupId>com.mulesoft.munit.tools</groupId>
    <artifactId>munit-maven-plugin</artifactId>
    <configuration>
        <runtimeConfiguration>
            <discoverRuntimes>
                <product>MULE_EE</product>  <!-- Invalid enum -->
            </discoverRuntimes>
        </runtimeConfiguration>
        <coverage>...</coverage>
    </configuration>
</plugin>

✅ GOOD (Simple configuration):
<plugin>
    <groupId>com.mulesoft.munit.tools</groupId>
    <artifactId>munit-maven-plugin</artifactId>
    <configuration>
        <!-- No runtimeConfiguration needed -->
        <!-- No munitTestsDirectory needed (auto-discovers src/test/munit/) -->
        <coverage>
            <runCoverage>true</runCoverage>
            <formats><format>html</format></formats>
        </coverage>
    </configuration>
</plugin>
```

**Why:** Parent POM configurations can conflict with explicit settings. Rely on MUnit's default auto-discovery for `src/test/munit/*-test-suite.xml` files.

